      "edition": "Sunday 18 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury update",
          "heading": "Manny Feyi-Waboso on track for Australia Test despite Exeter hamstring tweak",
          "body": "England's game-breaking wing Manny Feyi-Waboso should be fit for the Nations Championship Test against Australia despite tweaking a hamstring for Exeter against Newcastle. Initial scans showed no major damage, and Exeter's director of rugby Rob Baxter said \"there's nothing I'm hearing from our physios saying there should be a long-term issue\". Feyi-Waboso misses Exeter's Champions Cup opener at Toulouse, but early indications are said to be positive for a player with nine England tries since his 2024 Six Nations debut."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Wallabies 43-21",
