      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Police inquiry",
          "heading": "French prosecutors open probe into Lions lock Hyron Andrews' death",
          "body": "French authorities have opened an investigation into the death of Lions lock Hyron Andrews, 31, who was found unresponsive in a locked shower cubicle at the team hotel on the Île de Ré on Friday morning. La Rochelle public prosecutor Arnaud Laraize confirmed to AFP that the case is with the gendarmerie, which is treating it as a suspected accident pending an autopsy, and that there are no signs of violence on his body. The Lions confirmed they would play La Rochelle in Andrews' honour."
        },
        {
